          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            known as
            %em measurable Gelfand duality
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand-type duality
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
            and particular (
            %span.newWikiWord>
              σ-complete
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CF%83-complete+C%2A-algebra"} ?
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                point-free measure theory
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/point-free+measure+theory"} ?
          %p
            It is closely related to the usual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loomis-Sikorski+duality"} Loomis-Sikorski duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone-type
            counterpart.
          %h2#main_concepts Main concepts
          %p
            As in ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+duality"} Gelfand duality
            (as well as in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            and related fields), one wants to study the properties of a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            by means of the algebras of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            defined on them.
          %p
            In this case, the spaces we study are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+spaces"} measurable spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%83-algebra"} σ-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+function"} Bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+functions"} measurable functions
            on them form a particular algebraic structure (a commutative
            = succeed ")," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                σ-C*-algebra
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CF%83-C%5C%2A-algebra"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+of+an+adjunction"} center of the adjunction
          %h3#from_measurable_spaces_to_calgebras From measurable spaces to σ-C*-algebras
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^\infty(X)
            the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+function"} bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+functions"} measurable functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to\mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}^\infty
            forms a commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                σ-C*-algebra
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/%CF%83-C%5C%2A-algebra"} ?
          %p
            Given a measurable function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\mapsto h\circ f
            is a homomorphism of σ-C*-algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:\mathcal{L}^\infty(Y)\to \mathcal{L}^\infty(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Meas
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi σ
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Meas^{op}\to \sigma C^*Alg
          %h3#from_calgebras_to_measurable_spaces From σ-C*-algebras to measurable spaces
          %p
